  "answer": "Fish and frogs produce a huge number of eggs each year because they undergo external fertilization. In this process, the female lays a vast number of eggs in water, and the male releases millions of sperms to fertilize them. Since the fertilization happens outside the female's body and is influenced by natural factors, there is a high chance that many eggs may not get fertilized or may be lost due to environmental conditions. To ensure that enough offspring survive, these animals produce a large number of eggs each year.",
